<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="080" project="spaarke-side-pane-navigation-history-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Read-time security trimming — re-validate access, never render a cached name for an inaccessible record</title>
    <phase>8 Security &amp; retention verification</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Security-sensitive, legal-context frontend .tsx: cached labels for records the user has lost access to must never render (NFR-04); mishandling leaks names.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified read-time trim over already-built rows with a closed acceptance set; the judgment boundary is captured in an escalation trigger rather than requiring Opus.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Adds a render-time trim layer used by the tabs; Phase F peers (070/081/085) touch different surfaces — no shared-file contention.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>041,050</deps>
    <tags>security,frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Implement read-time security trimming for the Navigator: on render, re-validate the signed-in user's access to each history/pin target via a lightweight Xrm.WebApi retrieve, and drop or blank any row that returns 403/404 so a cached display name for a now-inaccessible record is never shown. Distinguish access denials (403/404) from transient network failures so an accessible row is not permanently dropped on a transient error.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with Power Apps security-model + Xrm.WebApi expertise, working in a legal (ethical-wall) context. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A render-time trimming layer applied to Recent/Pinned rows that re-validates access per target via a lightweight Xrm.WebApi retrieve and hides or blanks rows the user can no longer access (403/404), while leaving accessible rows intact and treating transient failures as non-authoritative. Includes tests covering the 403/404 vs transient distinction.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Per spec FR-12 + NFR-04 + plan.md Phase 8 task 080. History and pin rows carry cached display names; if a user loses access to a record, the cached name must not render (legal context). This task adds a lightweight per-target access re-check at render time and trims the rows accordingly.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/NavigatorPane/src/services/securityTrimService.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/NavigatorPane/src/tabs/RecentTab.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/NavigatorPane/src/tabs/PinnedTab.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/EventDetailSidePane/src/services/eventService.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/Notepad/src/hooks/useSprkMemoRepository.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="041" status="pending">Recent (Viewed) rows the trim layer re-validates before rendering.</dependency>
      <dependency task="050" status="pending">Pinned (Records) rows the trim layer re-validates before rendering.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">MUST security-trim cached labels at render time: never render a cached display name for a record the user can no longer access (FR-12 / NFR-04).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Host-context only — the access re-check uses a lightweight Xrm.WebApi retrieve under the signed-in user; no BFF, no plugin, no per-form web resource.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">A 403/404 (access lost / not found) trims the row; a transient network/timeout failure MUST NOT permanently drop an otherwise-accessible row — distinguish the two.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 tokens only; honor light/dark + --sprk-ui-scale; portal FluentProvider re-wrap for any portalled surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">Any @spaarke/ui-components code touched MUST stay React-16/17-safe: no createRoot; use JSXElement not JSX.Element.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <topic>Read-time security trimming via lightweight Xrm.WebApi retrieve + 403/404-vs-transient error handling in a legal context</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-portal-gotcha.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-side-pane-navigation-history-r1/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Lightweight retrieve + error parse" location="src/solutions/EventDetailSidePane/src/services/eventService.ts">Reuse the side-pane Xrm.WebApi retrieve + error-parse pattern for the per-target access re-check; inspect status to separate 403/404 from transient failures.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Batched retrieves" location="src/solutions/Notepad/src/hooks/useSprkMemoRepository.ts">Follow the existing retrieveMultiple/frame-walk shape when re-checking many targets efficiently.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor (FULL) + model-tier (sonnet) + effort (high) per task-execute Step 0.5; load the knowledge files and read the Recent/Pinned tabs + the reference services.</step>
    <step order="1">Create securityTrimService.ts: given a set of history/pin targets, perform a lightweight Xrm.WebApi retrieve per target (id-only / minimal columns) and classify each as accessible, denied (403/404), or transient-failure.</step>
    <step order="2">Apply the trim in RecentTab and PinnedTab render paths: rows classified denied are hidden or shown as "(no longer available)" with no cached name; accessible rows render normally.</step>
    <step order="3">For transient-failure rows, keep the row (do not permanently drop) — retry/degrade without leaking; only 403/404 trims.</step>
    <step order="4">Ensure a cached display name is never rendered for a denied target at any point (no flash of the cached name before the re-check resolves).</step>
    <step order="5">Author tests: a lost-access (403/404) target does not display its cached name (hidden or "(no longer available)"); accessible rows render normally; a transient error does NOT permanently drop an accessible row; light AND dark with portal re-wrap (ADR-021).</step>
    <step order="6">Recompile @spaarke/ui-components (if touched) + build the NavigatorPane; run tests; confirm green.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set task 080 status to completed.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/spaarke-side-pane-navigation-history-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a reliable access re-check cannot be performed client-side without first exposing the cached name (i.e., the name leaks before the re-check can hide it), STOP and escalate (root §6 — security-sensitive, legal-context) with the observed behavior and proposed alternatives rather than shipping a leak.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Lost-access record does not show its cached name (light and dark)">
      <steps>
        <step>Seed a history/pin row for a record, then simulate the user losing access (retrieve returns 403/404); render in light theme.</step>
        <step>Repeat in dark theme (data-theme=dark / prefers-color-scheme dark).</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The cached name is never rendered; the row is hidden or shown as "(no longer available)"; Fluent v9 tokens honor light and dark; portal FluentProvider re-wrap present (ADR-021).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Accessible rows render normally">
      <steps>
        <step>Render rows whose targets the user can access (retrieve succeeds).</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Accessible rows render normally with their names.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Transient error does not permanently drop an accessible row">
      <steps>
        <step>Simulate a transient network/timeout failure on the re-check for an accessible row.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The row is not permanently dropped (403/404 distinguished from transient); no cached name leaks.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Recompile @spaarke/ui-components (if touched) + build the NavigatorPane code page + run Jest tests.</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/NavigatorPane/src/services/securityTrimService.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/solutions/NavigatorPane/src/services/__tests__/securityTrimService.test.ts</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a record the user has lost access to, when history/pins render, then its cached name is not displayed (row hidden or shown as "(no longer available)").</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a record the user can access, when it renders, then the row renders normally with its name.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a transient network error on the re-check, when an accessible row is evaluated, then the row is NOT permanently dropped (403/404 distinguished from transient failure).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All tests pass; build green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Maps to spec FR-12 + NFR-04 + plan.md Phase 8 task 080. Legal-context sensitive: cached labels for inaccessible records must never render.</notes>
  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
